cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Semiotic Reasoning for Abstract Visual Tasks"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: 2024-12-31
url: "https://github.com/crystalline-labs/semiotic-arc"
repository-code: "https://github.com/crystalline-labs/semiotic-arc"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Cardwell
    given-names: Ryan
    affiliation: Crystalline Labs
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - abstract reasoning
  - visual cognition
  - semiotics
  - ARC-AGI
abstract: >
  A dual-channel cognitive architecture for abstract visual reasoning tasks,
  based on the insight that human visual cognition exploits both evolved
  (phylogenetically hardwired) pattern detectors and conditioned (ontogenetically
  learned) symbolic associations. Visual puzzles function as compressed reality
  models simulating physical, mathematical, or social phenomena.
